.TH netmeter 1  "netmeter 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
netmeter \- Local\-first LAN/WAN/TOTAL bandwidth meter (Linux)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnetmeter\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
NetMeter records local bandwidth usage in a background daemon and answers questions about TOTAL, LAN, and WAN usage. TOTAL comes from kernel interface counters; LAN is estimated from nftables when available and WAN is derived as TOTAL minus LAN. Use `netmeter status` to check whether the LAN/WAN split is available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
netmeter live
Live 1s dashboard (q to quit; no sudo needed)
.TP
netmeter show
Show historical usage
.TP
netmeter top
TOTAL\-only top talkers by iface or day
.TP
netmeter status
Daemon, database, and LAN/WAN split status
.TP
netmeter config
Read or change one configuration key at a time
.TP
netmeter export
Export raw samples as csv or json
.TP
netmeter import
Import vnStat daily history (runs vnstat \-\-json)
.TP
netmeter completions
Generate shell completions
.TP
netmeter manpage
Print the root roff man page to stdout
.TP
netmeter daemon
System daemon controls: run, start, stop, restart, install, uninstall
.TP
netmeter top-apps
TOTAL\-only per\-app history (day|week|month)
.TP
netmeter top-proc
TOTAL\-only per\-app dashboard (auto\-refreshing)
.TP
netmeter user-agent
Per\-user budget notifier (normally run as a systemd user unit)
.SH EXTRA

COMMON WORKFLOWS

Recorder and dashboards:
  sudo netmeter daemon install
  netmeter status
  netmeter live

History and top talkers:
  netmeter show \-\-period day
  netmeter show \-\-period month \-\-from 2026\-09\-01 \-\-json
  netmeter top \-\-by iface
  netmeter top\-apps \-\-period week
  netmeter top\-proc \-\-period day

Configuration (one key per command):
  netmeter config path
  netmeter config get [KEY]
  sudo netmeter config set budget_gb 2
  sudo netmeter config set budget_period month
  netmeter config reset

Budget notifications:
  systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now netmeter\-agent

Data movement:
  netmeter export \-\-from 2026\-09\-01 \-\-to 2026\-09\-07 \-\-format json
  netmeter import \-\-from vnstat

NOTES

`config set` accepts exactly one <KEY> <VALUE> pair; run it once per key.
`\-\-json` is command\-specific. `show`, `status`, and `top\-apps` include
`api_version`; `export \-\-format json` writes a bare JSON array.
